All with audio.click.

startIntro: close all modals; hide menu; intro.hidden=false; menu.hidden=true; scrollTop? window.
intro back → showMenu
intro begin → startNewGame

showScreen(name):
 const screens = {menu:screenMenu, intro:screenIntro, game:screenGame}
 hide all, show target; if menu new game etc.
 `body.classList.toggle('in-game', name==='game')` for potential CSS.
 For game, screenGame hidden false; hud etc.

showMenu():
 flow++; busy=false; game maybe keep? set null? Keep game for saves? On returning menu from pause we autosave. We can leave game object but menu; new game resets. Simpler set game=null after save? Load menu uses saves. Pause return menu → autosave, game=null; selected. Hide modals. show screen menu. Update menu save count. Audio close.
 Start menu: screen-menu is-active class. Others hidden.
 Reset menu animations? CSS screen fade only game. Add class.

startNewGame():
 flow++;
 game = new Conquest();
 selected = game.state.playerPos;
 targeting=null; busy=false;
