 hostLocation
 hostTroops
 blessing chip hidden toggle
 recruit.disabled etc
 fortify.disabled = busy || !game? etc.
 endturn disabled busy/outcome; label busy ? 'The Hollow moves…' : 'End Turn'
 pause/sound disabled? sound fine.
 objective text: outcome? else "Seize the Shadow Citadel"
Maybe include current province host location.

renderProvince:
 if no game return
 p = PROVINCES[selected]
 owner = ...
 owner badge text: Dawn/Hollow/Free; className `owner-badge owner-badge--player` etc.
 name, flavor, garrison, income '+'+p.income, defence game.defenseLabel.
 If targeting:
   note = choose target; action hidden? Show action maybe disabled. Let's handle:
   action.hidden = true; note text = `Choose a province for ${POWERS[targeting].name}.`; class is-ready.
 else:
   const act = game.actionFor(selected)
   if (selected===playerPos && owner==='player') { action.hidden=true; note "Your host is stationed here. Select a neighbouring province to march."; }
   else if (act.type==='none') { action.hidden=false; action.disabled=true; label act.label; note ...}
   else:
     action.hidden=false; disabled false; textContent = act.label; 
     note = if attack: `Forecast: your host ${host}${bless?' (blessed)':''} against a defence of ${act.power}.` + (act.risky ? ' A hard fight.' : ' The Dawn has the advantage.');
     class is-warn/is-ready.
   If owner player and not host: note += ' Held in the Dawn's name · +X faith.'
 Province note: set text and classes.
 action onclick handled globally once, not re-bound in render (avoid duplicate). Bind once at init. It reads current selected.

renderPowers:
 buttons each: toggle is-used based on usedPowers; is-active targeting; is-poor faith<cost; disabled = busy || outcome || used || faith<cost? If disabled, click won't fire; but we want click to show message for insufficient. Better don't set disabled, just classes; handler checks and toasts. But a11y: aria-disabled true. Use btn.setAttribute('aria-disabled', ...). Keep pointer.
